INT. EDIT SUITE - LATE NIGHT

Two monitors. A timeline with a red marker at 00:41:12. LENA (30s), editor, has her feet on the desk. The director, OBI (40s), is standing.

OBI
Cut twelve. Tell me why you pulled the interview about her suicide attempt.

LENA
I did not pull it. I moved it. Watch.

She scrubs. On the monitor, a woman, ADAEZE (50s), sits in a garden.

ADAEZE (ON MONITOR)
People want one reason. There was never one reason. There were a dozen small things and then there was a Tuesday. What changed it was that my neighbour knocked. She did not have a speech. She had soup, and she stayed until my daughter came.

Lena pauses it.

LENA
If we put her before the archive footage, the film says what she says: it was complicated, and somebody knocking on the door mattered. If we put her after, it plays like an epilogue and everyone has stopped listening.

OBI
And the counsellor interview?

LENA
Stays. Right after her. Recovery is the spine of the film, not the coda.

Obi looks at the timeline for a long moment.

OBI
Do we have the card at the end? The number?

LENA
Not yet. Graphics have not sent it.

OBI
Then we do not have a cut.

FADE OUT.
